e=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Various+Licenses+and+Comments+about+Them&amp;rft.atitle=Apache+License%2C+Version+2.0&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.gnu.org%2Flicenses%2Flicense-list.html%23apache2&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AApache+License\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-osi-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-osi_3-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical\">\"OSI-approved licenses by name David Gutierrez &amp; David Louie Gutierrez\"</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Open_Source_Initiative\" title=\"Open Source Initiative\">Open Source Initiative</a>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20110428141712/http://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical\">Archived</a> from the original on 28 April 2011<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">31 March</span> 2011</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=OSI-approved+licenses+by+name+David+Gutierrez+%26+David+Louie+Gutierrez&amp;rft.pub=Open+Source+Initiative&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.opensource.org%2Flicenses%2Falphabetical&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AApache+License\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-nmr-permissive-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-nmr-permissive_4-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFNew&#95;Media&#95;Rights2008\" class=\"citation web cs1\">New Media Rights (12 September 2008). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.newmediarights.org/open_source/new_media_rights_open_source_licensing_guide\">\"Open Source Licensing Guide\"</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/California_Western_School_of_Law\" title=\"California Western School of Law\">California Western School of Law</a><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">28 November</span> 2015</span>. <q><i>The 'BSD-like' licenses such as the BSD, MIT, and Apache licenses are extremely permissive, requiring little more than attributing the original portions of the licensed code to the original developers in your own code and/or documentation.</i></q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Open+Source+Licensing+Guide&amp;rft.pub=California+Western+School+of+Law&amp;rft.date=2008-09-12&amp;rft.au=New+Media+Rights&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.newmediarights.org%2Fopen&#95;source%2Fnew&#95;media&#95;rights&#95;open&#95;source&#95;licensing&#95;guide&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AApache+License\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐c4q88\nCached time: 20260918180909\nCache expiry: 1057861\nCache expiry source: Template:Years_or_months_ago (currentmonth)\nReduced expiry: true\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.290 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.458 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 956/1000000\nRevision size: 2889/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 19102/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1809/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 18/100\nExpensive parser function count: 3/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11142/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.170/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 4310326/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTra